# Rule: commands the agent may run without asking

This rule is not file-scoped, so it has no `.claude/rules/` adapter. Claude Code enforces it through `permissions.allow` in `.claude/settings.json`; `AGENTS.md` "Rules" lists it for every other agent.

{{OWNER}} authorizes the agent to run these commands without asking each time:

<!-- kit:if has.typecheck -->
- `{{CMD_TYPECHECK}}`
<!-- kit:end -->
<!-- kit:if has.lint -->
- `{{CMD_LINT}}`
<!-- kit:end -->
<!-- kit:if has.test -->
- `{{CMD_TEST}}`
<!-- kit:end -->
- `git status`, `git diff`, `git log`, `git show`, `git add`, `git commit`

<!-- kit:adapt: Add the project's safe local commands (install dependencies, start the dev server, start or stop local services, a production build that only writes local files), one bullet each with a short comment. Never add a command that reaches production. -->

When this list and `.claude/settings.json` disagree, the stricter one applies; fix the other in the same PR.

Any command outside this list, and any command that rewrites git history, deletes files, or changes external infrastructure, needs {{OWNER}}'s confirmation first. Commands that reach production (ssh to a server, deploys, data scripts that write to a production database) are never on this list.
